WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:04.961
If you would've told us in 2011 that the third
sequel in the Thor franchise would be the

00:00:04.961 --> 00:00:08.090
one of the funniest movies of the year on
its release, there wouldn't have been a lot

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:08.980
of reason to believe you.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:14.380
Yet here we are, with Thor: Ragnarok earning
over $120 million on its opening weekend,

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:18.980
and rave reviews crowning it as the most hilarious
entry in the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:23.760
One of the best comedic moments in the entire
MCU occurred during The Avengers, a movie

00:00:23.769 --> 00:00:28.070
which, apart from the Iron Man series, was
really the entry in the franchise that proved

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:32.540
Marvel's heroes to be as deft with their comedic
timing as they were with landing punches.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:37.450
We're talking, of course, about Hulk vs. Loki,
specifically when the green guy absolutely

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:39.580
thrashes the cocky Asgardian god …

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:43.260
"Puny God."

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:48.440
Trailers for Thor: Ragnarok teased the reunion
of Loki with Hulk, the only Avenger who can

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:51.540
be said to have truly—and humiliatingly—defeated
him.

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:56.100
But while the two do team up by the movie's
end, Thor: Ragnarok was originally supposed

00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:00.440
to address their contentious relationship
in a more direct, hands-on way, with a hilarious

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:03.880
callback to The Avengers that reportedly had
test audiences howling.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:08.150
According to Empire, there was originally
a moment near the end of Thor: Ragnarok where

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:12.670
Hulk, Thor, and Loki all line up beside each
other before Hulk, still harboring no love

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:15.380
for Loki, unexpectedly punches him out of
the frame.

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:19.880
The callback actually served a dual function,
referencing Hulk and Loki's past encounter

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:22.980
while mirroring a similar sucker punch Hulk
once pulled on Thor.

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:28.520
Director Taika Waititi says viewers loved
the moment, but it was ultimately cut for

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:29.600
the purposes of time.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:33.980
Evidently, it made people laugh a little too
hard, derailing the momentum of the scene.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:36.800
Waititi explained the content of the missing
scene to Empire.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:39.860
"They all land on the bridge—Thor, Loki
and then Hulk.

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:41.000
They stand for a second.

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:44.860
Then Hulk just smashes Loki, punches him out
of the frame—just like in Avengers, when

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:45.930
Hulk did it to Thor.

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:48.740
It was a crowd favorite, but we just had to
get rid of it for time.

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:50.120
It might be on the DVD."

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:54.400
Get your laughs in now, because when Avengers:
Infinity War hits theaters, it won't be a

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:56.440
lighthearted romp... that's for sure.

00:01:56.990 --> 00:01:57.980
Thanks for watching!

00:01:57.990 --> 00:02:00.140
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:02.360
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

